            "review_text": "Traveler02682362214\n8 contributions\n2\nA delicious and relaxing restaurant!\nFeb 2026 • Family\nA temple restaurant that makes you feel at ease - Phuc An temple restaurant (Vung Tau)\nIn the hectic daily life of Vung Tau, Phuc An Shoji restaurant is a naturally soothing place. It's not flashy, but the interior is clean, rustic and warm and peaceful from the moment you enter.\nEach dish is very carefully prepared, seasoned gently and naturally, and without too much oil or seasoning. After eating, the body feels light and the mind feels ready. Every dish is homely, simple yet profound. Herbal teas and healthy drinks were also very refreshing and impressive.\nWhat stuck with me most was the personality of the people at the shop. They are very kind and sincere, and feel as if they have visited an acquaintance's house.\nThe prices are reasonable and the food quality is stable. Phuoc An Shojin restaurant is not just a place to eat, it is an important place to regain balance between mind and body. This is one of the places I would definitely recommend stopping by when visiting Vung Tau, and I would definitely like to visit again myself.\nRead more\nTranslated from Japanese\nShow original\nWritten February 5, 2026",
